{
  "configuration_id": "config_009",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_021 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) achieved 0.5266 acc, while config_028 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) achieved only 0.2079 acc. This shows the multimodal setup substantially outperforms image-only, but we cannot yet determine whether RNA alone is the primary driver or whether the fusion of both modalities is essential. Uncertainty: We lack an RNA-only baseline with the same encoder (pca_n2000) and profile setting (singleprofile) to isolate the image's marginal contribution. This experiment (config_009: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the cleanest control for config_021, changing only the model setting from multimodal to rna_only while holding the RNA encoder and profile setting constant. It will clarify whether to prioritize improving the image encoder (if RNA alone is weak, fusion matters) or the RNA encoder/aggregation (if RNA alone is strong, the image is secondary). Under a limited budget, this single-variable comparison maximizes information gain about the most consequential design choice—modality contribution—before investing in more complex multiprofile or aggregation variants."
}

